# React SSE Integration Rules

## Server-Sent Events Implementation

**Authentication Challenge**: Browser EventSource doesn't support custom headers - use polyfill for JWT authentication.

**Connection Management**: Handle reconnection, cleanup, and connection lifecycle properly in React components.

**Real-time State Updates**: Implement incremental state building for streaming content.

## JWT Authentication for SSE

### Option 1: EventSource Polyfill (RECOMMENDED)
```javascript
import { EventSourcePolyfill } from 'event-source-polyfill';

const eventSource = new EventSourcePolyfill("/api/stream_ai_response", {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
});
eventSource.onmessage = onMessageHandler;
```

### Option 2: Query Parameter (Simple but less secure)
```javascript
const eventSource = new EventSource(`/api/stream_ai_response?token=${jwtToken}`);
```

### Option 3: fetch-event-source Alternative
```javascript
import { fetchEventSource } from '@microsoft/fetch-event-source';

fetchEventSource('/api/stream_ai_response', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
    onmessage(event) {
        // Handle message
    }
});
```

## React Integration Pattern

### Basic SSE Hook Implementation
```jsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

function useAiStream(prompt, token) {
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const [isComplete, setIsComplete] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!prompt || !token) return;

    const source = new EventSourcePolyfill("/api/stream_ai_response", {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
    });

    source.onmessage = (event) => {
      try {
        const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
        if (data.content) {
          // Incremental content building
          setMessage(prev => prev + data.content);
        }
      } catch(err) {
        console.error("Failed to parse SSE data", err);
        setError("Failed to parse response");
      }
    };

    source.addEventListener("done", () => {
      setIsComplete(true);
      source.close();
    });

    source.addEventListener("error", (event) => {
      const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
      setError(data.error);
      source.close();
    });

    source.onerror = (err) => {
      console.error("SSE connection error:", err);
      setError("Connection error");
      source.close();
    };

    // Cleanup on unmount
    return () => {
      source.close();
    };
  }, [prompt, token]);

  return { message, isComplete, error };
}
```

## Message Handling Patterns

### Incremental Content Building
```jsx
// For KI streaming - append each chunk
setMessage(prev => prev + data.content);

// For structured updates - merge objects
setData(prev => ({ ...prev, ...data }));

// For list updates - append to array
setItems(prev => [...prev, data.item]);
```

### Event Type Handling
```javascript
// Standard data events
source.onmessage = (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // Handle regular data
};

// Named events from Django
source.addEventListener("done", (event) => {
  // Stream completed
  source.close();
});

source.addEventListener("error", (event) => {
  const errorData = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // Handle server-sent errors
});

source.addEventListener("ping", (event) => {
  // Keep-alive ping - ignore or log
});
```

## Connection Lifecycle Management

### Component Integration
```jsx
function AiStreamComponent({ prompt }) {
  const token = useAuthToken();
  const { message, isComplete, error } = useAiStream(prompt, token);

  if (error) {
    return <div className="error">Error: {error}</div>;
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {message ? (
        <pre className="whitespace-pre-wrap">{message}</pre>
      ) : (
        <div className="loading">Waiting for AI response...</div>
      )}
      {isComplete && <div className="status">Stream completed</div>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Manual Connection Control
```jsx
function ControlledStream() {
  const [source, setSource] = useState(null);
  const [isConnected, setIsConnected] = useState(false);

  const startStream = () => {
    const newSource = new EventSourcePolyfill("/api/stream", {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
    });
    
    newSource.onopen = () => setIsConnected(true);
    newSource.onerror = () => setIsConnected(false);
    
    setSource(newSource);
  };

  const stopStream = () => {
    if (source) {
      source.close();
      setSource(null);
      setIsConnected(false);
    }
  };

  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      if (source) source.close();
    };
  }, [source]);

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={startStream} disabled={isConnected}>
        Start Stream
      </button>
      <button onClick={stopStream} disabled={!isConnected}>
        Stop Stream
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Error Handling & Reconnection

### Automatic Reconnection Logic
```javascript
function useSSEWithReconnect(url, options) {
  const [reconnectCount, setReconnectCount] = useState(0);
  const maxReconnects = 5;

  useEffect(() => {
    let source;
    let reconnectTimeout;

    const connect = () => {
      source = new EventSourcePolyfill(url, options);
      
      source.onerror = (error) => {
        source.close();
        
        if (reconnectCount < maxReconnects) {
          const delay = Math.pow(2, reconnectCount) * 1000; // Exponential backoff
          reconnectTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
            setReconnectCount(prev => prev + 1);
            connect();
          }, delay);
        }
      };
    };

    connect();

    return () => {
      if (source) source.close();
      if (reconnectTimeout) clearTimeout(reconnectTimeout);
    };
  }, [url, reconnectCount]);
}
```

### Connection Status Indication
```jsx
function StreamStatus({ isConnected, error, reconnectCount }) {
  if (error) {
    return <div className="status error">Connection Error: {error}</div>;
  }
  
  if (!isConnected && reconnectCount > 0) {
    return <div className="status warning">Reconnecting... (Attempt {reconnectCount})</div>;
  }
  
  if (isConnected) {
    return <div className="status success">Connected</div>;
  }
  
  return <div className="status">Connecting...</div>;
}
```

## Performance Considerations

### Memory Management
- Always close EventSource in cleanup functions
- Avoid creating new connections on every render
- Use useMemo for connection options if they contain complex objects
- Clear message buffers when appropriate to prevent memory leaks

### State Optimization
- Use functional state updates for appending content: `setState(prev => prev + newData)`
- Debounce rapid updates if messages come too frequently
- Consider using useReducer for complex state transitions
- Implement message deduplication if server might send duplicates